{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Settings.Nondeterminism_strictness</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"hegel","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Hegel","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Settings","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Nondeterminism_strictness","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>How a run handles nondeterministic test behavior. In <code>hegel.toml</code>: <code>quiet</code>, <code>warn</code>, or <code>error</code>.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span><span> = </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-t.Quiet\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Quiet\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Quiet</span></span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>Switch to nondeterministic handling silently.</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li><li id=\"type-t.Warn\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Warn\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Warn</span></span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p><code>Quiet</code>, but print a notice per run.</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li><li id=\"type-t.Error\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.Error\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Error</span></span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>Abort the run with a flaky-test error.</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li></ol></div></div>"}